{% markdown %}

Every post needs a hero image. Sometimes you don't need the perfect one -- you just need something that doesn't clash. Stock photos give you random results. AI generation gives you consistent ones.

The model I'm using is [FLUX.2-dev](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-dev) via [Together AI](https://www.together.ai/), running about a penny per image. But the model isn't the trick -- the style constraint is.

## The style is the whole trick

Japanese blockprint aesthetic: high-contrast black ink woodcut on cream paper, sparse warm amber accent, no gradients. Every prompt gets the same style prefix baked in.

A limited palette reads as a deliberate choice, not a generated artifact. High contrast holds up at small sizes and in dark mode. The consistency across posts starts to look like a set -- not a random pile of AI images.

