The other rule I settled on: abstract subjects only. Sailboats, paths through grass, kites with cut strings. Think about the feeling of the post, not its subject matter. "A magnifying glass over scattered dots" works better for a search post than "a search results page." FLUX.2-dev can't render text anyway, which honestly helps -- no temptation to put words on the image.

## The generator

I built a [small browser tool](/image-generator/) that lives in the site itself. Paste your Together AI key, type a subject, hit Generate -- three images run in parallel in about 20-30 seconds. Click one, drag the corners to crop, save straight to `src/site/images/blog/`. The tool outputs a frontmatter snippet ready to paste.

The URL updates as you change options, so any setup is bookmarkable. Advanced options expose the style prefix, negative prompt, steps, and dimensions -- useful for experimenting without touching config files.

About 20 diffusion steps is the sweet spot: results look the same as 28 to 35 but generate noticeably faster. Three images per post runs about $0.03. The approach is [on GitHub](https://github.com/khawkins98/allaboutken-11ty/tree/main/scripts/image-generate) if you want to adapt it.

